ation, multi-step vendor approval) can exceed 90 days even though some competitors (e.g., GovAccess) offer free instant scans as a lead-gen/self-serve entry point that could shorten this for smaller municipalities.\",\n      \"obligations\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T8\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Two one-time setup items beyond baseline SaaS legal docs: (1) government vendor/procurement registration requirements vary by state/municipality (e.g., W-9, SAM.gov equivalents, state e-procurement portal registration) and may need review before first government sale; (2) marketing/compliance-claim language needs legal review to avoid FTC false-advertising exposure of the type levied against accessiBe ($1M fine) for overstating that automated scans/tools guarantee full ADA/WCAG compliance.\",\n      \"obligations\": [\n        \"State/local government vendor registration and procurement portal onboarding (jurisdiction-specific, one-time per state)\",\n        \"Legal review of marketing/compliance-claim language to avoid FTC false-advertising liability for overstating automated compliance guarantees\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"competitors\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"GovAccess\",\n      \"url\": \"https://govaccess.us/\",\n      \"relationship\": \"direct\",\n      \"pricing\": null,\n      \"evidence\": \"Free automated WCAG 2.1 AA scan for government sites, built on axe-core, positioned explicitly around ADA Title II deadline for municipalities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Quillinox\",\n      \"url\": \"https://quillinox.com/\",\n      \"relationship\": \"direct\",\n      \"pricing\": null,\n      \"evidence\": \"Full ADA Title II compliance platform for local government: scanning, PDF remediation, compliance defense package, grievance management, audit trail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CivicPlus / AudioEye\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.civicplus.com/web-accessibility-software/\",\n      \"relationship\": \"direct\",\n      \"pricing\": null